<p>
  The free plan is free permanently, not a trial that runs out. It has four
  monthly or standing limits and one storage cap, and this page says exactly
  how each one is counted. Your live figures are always on
  <strong>Settings &rarr; Usage</strong>.
</p>

<h2>The limits</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong><%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %> completed documents a month.</strong> A document counts the first time <em>any</em> signer completes it. A two-signer document counts once, when the first of them finishes.</li>
  <li><strong><%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_SENDS_PER_MONTH %> documents sent a month.</strong> Every document created for signature is a send, however it was started &mdash; the recipients form, a share link, "sign it yourself" or a correction.</li>
  <li><strong><%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_IN_FLIGHT %> documents out for signature at once.</strong> A live count, not a monthly one: it goes down again as soon as a document completes, is declined, expires or is deleted.</li>
  <li><strong><%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_SEATS %> user.</strong> Inviting a second person needs the paid plan &mdash; see <%= link_to 'Teams and seats', help_article_path('teams-and-seats') %>.</li>
  <li><strong><%= number_to_human_size(Quotas::Limits::FREE_STORAGE_BYTES) %> of storage.</strong> Everything the account holds, counted once each. The paid plan gives <%= number_to_human_size(Quotas::Limits::PAID_STORAGE_BYTES_PER_SEAT) %> per seat.</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Free accounts also carry an EsignCenter footer on the emails we send for you
  and on the pages your signers sign on. Everything else about signing &mdash;
  the sealed PDF, the audit trail, public verification, Word uploads, signing
  order, decline and delegate, email verification for signers &mdash; is the
  same on both plans.
</p>

<h2>What happens when you reach one</h2>

<p>
  Nothing is deleted and nothing is lost. New documents cannot be started until
  the month resets, and a share link answers visitors with a polite "not
  accepting responses right now". Documents already out for signature always
  finish: reaching a limit never strands somebody halfway through signing, and
  that completion is still recorded. Downloads and exports keep working.
</p>

<p>
  We email your account's administrators once when you reach
  <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_COMPLETIONS_WARNING_AT %> of
  <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %> completions, so the ceiling
  is never a surprise.
</p>

<aside class="help-callout">
  <p>
    <strong>Good to know:</strong> correcting a document somebody has already
    signed never costs a second completion, however many rounds it takes, and
    it is allowed even when you have used all
    <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %> &mdash; which is usually
    exactly when a mistake is spotted. It does count as one of your
    <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_SENDS_PER_MONTH %> sends.
  </p>
</aside>

<h2>Resets, storage and upgrades</h2>

<p>
  The monthly counts run on the UTC calendar month and reset by themselves at
  midnight UTC on the first. There is nothing to press.
</p>

<p>
  Storage is the one cap that never stops you sending or signing &mdash; only
  new uploads are refused when you are full. To free space, delete what you no
  longer need and then <strong>delete permanently</strong> from the archive;
  the ordinary delete only archives, and archived files still count.
</p>

<p>
  Upgrading lifts the document limits at once. If you later drop back to the
  free plan, your free month starts the moment the paid plan ends: you begin at
  0 of <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_COMPLETIONS_PER_MONTH %> completions and 0 of
  <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_SENDS_PER_MONTH %> sends, and nothing is deleted.
  See <%= link_to 'Billing and your free trial', help_article_path('billing-and-trial') %>
  and the <%= link_to 'pricing page', pricing_path %>.
</p>
